# std/write — one of the file tools (std/files holds the source they share).
# The help is a HERE-STRING so it lives in this expression, which is stripped
# from the tree the build sees: editing the docs re-keys this tool's ArgTree and
# nothing it builds from.
HELP=<<END
Write a file, creating it and any missing directories, or replacing it. `root` is the file, such as sources/repo/99-dirty/README.md. Prefer this over heredocs and redirection via bash. Writing inside a source tree makes a child commit of it.
@param content The full new file content.
@writer
@root
END
IMAGE=run --base:@=DEEP-DEPS/rustc --src:@=DEEP-DEPS/files
curry --base=$IMAGE --op=write --help=$HELP
